# Every bit here is architecturally implied by a CPU that reports SSE2.
# A game testing a MASK of leaf-1 EDX bits fails if ANY of them is missing,
# which is why "SSE2 is advertised" does not settle the Burnout question.
MAXL  !0
FPU   0x1
# DE (debugging extensions) and PSE (page size extension): present on every real
# x86 since the Pentium. FEX 2607/2608 reports 0 for both.
DE    0x1
PSE   0x1
TSC   0x1
CX8   0x1
CMOV  0x1
MMX   0x1
SSE   0x1
SSE2  0x1
SSE3  0x1
